      ],
      "description": "[expert] StubFalsifier's backing temp file is unlinked immediately after construction (line 78). If StubFalsifier lazily reads from the file path on each falsify() call rather than caching the contents in memory, every subsequent judge.falsify(sf) in the main loop will read from a deleted file and raise FileNotFoundError or silently fall back to a default. The try/finally ensures cleanup even if the constructor raises, which is good, but the real engine doesn't have this problem (it passes config in-memory). Verify that StubFalsifier reads the file once at __init__ time; if it doesn't, move the unlink to a destructor or use an atexit handler.",
