      "description": "[expert] If all items fail as INFRA (every LLMInvokeError increments infra, agree stays 0), total > 0 and the percentage computation on line 208 is safe. However, agree / total on line 211 is integer division in Python 3 (both are int), always yielding 0 or 1, never a fraction. The result is correct only because 0/total < 0.9 and total/total >= 0.9, but the float division on line 208 (100.0 * agree / total) and the int division on line 211 use different semantics. Consider using agree / total >= args.min_agree with explicit float or making agree and total floats for consistency with the 0.9 threshold.",
